<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kilij Arslan IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1265</span> · Also known as Rukn al-Din Kilij Arslan IV</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kilij Arslan IV was sultan of the Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> from 1248, under Mongol overlordship, at first alongside his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaykaus-ii">Kaykaus II</a> and Kayqubad II. Backed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, he became sole ruler after Kaykaus II fled in 1261, but real power lay with the minister known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muin-al-din-suleyman-pervane">Pervane</a>, who had him put to death in 1265.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kilij-arslan-iv.jpg" alt="Kilij Arslan IV" width="320" height="149" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rare_coin_of_Kilij_Arslan_IV,_ruler_of_the_Sultanate_of_Rum._Minted_at_Sivas_in_1248_or_1249.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
